{"skill":{"slug":"web-search-ex-skill","displayName":"Web Search"},"version":{"version":"1.3.0","createdAt":1773108175408,"changelog":"- Added detailed SKILL.md with updated description, usage examples, parameters, and output formats.\n- Clarified support for multiple search engines (Baidu, Bing, DuckDuckGo) with smart fallback and no API key required.\n- Documented error handling, dependency requirements, and search strategy.\n- Provided clear code examples for search, deep search, and webpage crawling.\n- Outlined input/output formats and execution settings for better integration guidance.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3141,"sha256":"ad25f3cf06badd9701a61c5f0c467623c8c8a838a59e65615de09ed7f63c46c5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":281,"sha256":"3fd71405be7f310d1f60a6bd0e12d2bac90d9f213f46750a8d6f14798c010ba5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/__init__.py","size":160,"sha256":"9a3c3bc2c0f9a7ba440a45dd5f69e9539eb5d973842f9fdf84b40cc8da39357d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/web_search.py","size":17694,"sha256":"798fc76c3877f5b78e63e1da04c76af512c25e3b57893188cb47a3914be608d8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"setup.py","size":1550,"sha256":"7aa25b56f5a360dc57d6bddf41c2dc5967b36d9951efddf5de04b5bdcd1d1b32","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2169,"sha256":"1858064a558c67c2248022f8ea4597377db671338bf55b3cede7d7f070464a44","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789134096896,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"147fe162d21c6d26cee15060fce4f7ddf1bfe5b6559673384a5e1409ebb2d576","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/147fe162d21c6d26cee15060fce4f7ddf1bfe5b6559673384a5e1409ebb2d576","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085840398},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":21,"checkedAt":1789134096896},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This web-search skill is mostly coherent, but it needs Review because its crawler can fetch arbitrary URLs from the host environment without network-scope safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Internet access, scraping, and browser automation fit a web-search/crawl tool, but unrestricted crawling is not proportionately contained for agent environments that may reach internal services.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses open-ended runtime dependency ranges for uv, requests, baidusearch, crawl4ai, and playwright with no lockfile or hashes; setup.py consumes those requirements directly.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"User-facing instructions disclose crawling and deep search, but they do not define allowed destinations, private-network exclusions, redirect handling, or a privacy warning for sending queries and URLs to external search engines and target sites.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, memory writes, privilege escalation, credential harvesting, or destructive file operations were found; Playwright's first-run Chromium download is disclosed and purpose-aligned.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is web search and it openly documents search, deep_search, and crawl actions, but the crawl path is a broad network-fetch capability that can retrieve content from any http(s) URL reachable by the runtime.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only in an environment where outbound crawling is sandboxed away from localhost, private networks, cloud metadata endpoints, and sensitive internal services. Avoid sending secrets, private URLs, or confidential queries through it, and prefer pinned dependencies or a reviewed lockfile before production use.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded: SKILL.md documents deep_search and Web Page Crawling, so the capability is not hidden, though its breadth is still relevant to the Review verdict.\n[LP3] expected: Network and browser automation are expected for this skill, but the artifact lacks an explicit permission boundary for crawler network reach.\n[SQP-2] expected: External transmission of search queries and crawl URLs is inherent to the advertised function, but the documentation should warn users not to submit sensitive or internal-only data.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-region default is documented, and Baidu is a listed engine, but code also hard-codes zh-CN headers and cn.bing while the region parameter is not meaningfully applied.\n[SDI-1] expected: Deep search and page crawling are documented features; the concern is accepted only as overbroad active fetching without destination controls.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted: the crawl action validates only scheme and length before passing the URL to AsyncWebCrawler and returning fetched content.\n[SC1] unexpected: Accepted as a hardening issue: runtime dependencies use lower-bound ranges rather than exact reviewed versions.\n[SC4] unexpected: Accepted as an unverifiable dependency issue; no artifact evidence shows the named dependencies are intentionally malicious.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: unrestricted crawl can act as a host-side fetch of attacker-supplied http(s) URLs, with response content returned.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted as supply-chain risk from unpinned dependencies consumed by setup.py, not as evidence of a malicious package.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789134096896}}}}}